            {
              "type": "note",
              "id": "m1Qsu",
              "name": "Tooltip behaviour",
              "width": 320,
              "height": 330,
              "content": "Tooltip (ADR-0017, Tokens > Tooltip): every control whose state needs a reason. Timing and placement from Material Design: opens 300 ms after the pointer rests on the control (fade in and grow from 0.8, 150 ms), stays 100 ms after it leaves (moving to another control switches the text at once), fades out in 75 ms. Centered under the control, a pointer on its edge aimed at the control and 4 px from it, above it (pointer down) when there is no room below, on the roomier side when neither has room, 8 px from the window edges; near a side edge, aligned with the control's start or end (here: the button's end). Stays inside the window, never takes clicks. Shown on disabled controls too: that is when the reason matters most. Raised panel: surface-raised, border-raised outline, shadow (lighter tone for elevation, as Material does in dark mode). Text: font-size-caption, text-primary, wraps at 220 px."
            }
          ]
        },
