              "letterSpacing": 1,
              "fontStyle": "italic"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "aqnJ3",
              "name": "Rule",
              "fill": "$text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "On every move between screens, a cursor erases the headline, then types the title of the next screen, like a game console. Erase 10 ms per character, type 18 ms per character, each phase 150 ms at most; the cursor stays 120 ms after the last character, then goes. Meanwhile the leading slot fades through (out, swap at the midpoint, in) over the 200 ms of the screen transition. Same for a lateral move (SETTINGS → ABOUT). With Windows' Animation effects off: no cursor, the headline swaps at once.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": "$font-size-body",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
